From: LinBox <linbox@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] LinBox box64: Android RELR tags in elfparser32.c (32-bit twin)

32-bit twin of 0002/0003. The file only exists since v0.3.2 (v0.3.0 has no
32-bit loader) and its DT_RELR case indentation is identical in v0.3.2
through v0.4.5, so a single variant covers all tags that have the file.
On v0.3.0 the file is absent, the dry-run fails and the patch is skipped.
The hunk headers carry v0.4.4 line numbers; patch locates the
(unique) anchors by scanning, so line drift across tags is fine. A hunk that
cannot find its anchors fails the dry-run and is skipped whole
(patchOptional=1 in build.sh) - it is NEVER force-placed at a wrong offset.

---
diff --git a/src/elfs/elfparser32.c b/src/elfs/elfparser32.c
--- a/src/elfs/elfparser32.c
+++ b/src/elfs/elfparser32.c
@@ -213,2 +213,3 @@
                 case DT_RELR:
+                case 0x6fffe000:  // DT_ANDROID_RELR (LinBox: bionic RELR tags, same encoding)
                     h->relr = ptr;
@@ -216,2 +217,3 @@
                 case DT_RELRSZ:
+                case 0x6fffe001:  // DT_ANDROID_RELRSZ
                     h->relrsz = val;
@@ -219,2 +221,3 @@
                 case DT_RELRENT:
+                case 0x6fffe003:  // DT_ANDROID_RELRENT
                     h->relrent = val;
